    <h1>Christmas Carol Goes Wrong</h1>

    
    
        
        
    <div  class="bard-content">
        <p><strong>WHAT A BUNCH OF DICKENS</strong></p><p><span style="color: rgb(24, 23, 25);">The Cornley Amateur Drama Society return with tidings of chaos and joy, ready to tackle the </span><strong>Charles Dickens</strong><span style="color: rgb(24, 23, 25);">’ classic, </span><em>A Christmas Carol</em><span style="color: rgb(24, 23, 25);">. With no hope of a silent night, disaster strikes with hilarious consequences.</span></p><p><strong><em>Christmas Carol Goes Wrong</em></strong><span style="color: rgb(24, 23, 25);"> is ‘a Dickensian disaster to savour’ (Guardian), returning for a limited 6 week run in London’s West End following last year’s sold-out season. Do not miss </span><strong>Dave Hearn</strong><span style="color: rgb(24, 23, 25);"> as Max, original cast of <em>The Play That Goes Wrong</em> and the BBC comedy series <em>The Goes Wrong Show</em>, returning to the West End. Also, MISCHIEF originals <strong>Henry Lewis</strong> and <strong>Jonathan Sayer </strong>will join the cast as their original Cornley characters Robert and Dennis for two weeks from 14 - 23 January 2027.</span></p><p><span style="color: rgb(24, 23, 25);">Give the gift of laughter to your family and see this ‘irresistible Christmas treat’ (WhatsOnStage) from the multi award-winning company MISCHIEF.</span></p><p><span style="color: rgb(24, 23, 25);">The Cornley crew battle miscommunication, delays to their set, actors missing in action and a growing feud over who will play the lead. It’s sure to be a disastrous take on the much-loved classic Christmas story of Ebenezer Scrooge. Will Cornley finally change their ways, or will their misfortunes wreak havoc yet again.</span></p><p><span style="color: rgb(24, 23, 25);">Enjoy MISCHIEF’s festive slice of pure escapism at the worst production in Christmas past, present and yet to come!</span></p><p><strong>DON’T BE A SCROOGE, BOOK TICKETS TODAY</strong></p>
    </div>


    
        
        







    
    




    








    
    
    




    



